# Skill Enhancer

This project has the skill-enhancer skill at
`skills/skill-enhancer/SKILL.md` in this repo (or wherever you copied
the `skills/skill-enhancer/` folder). Read that file in full before
auditing or improving a skill.

Quick reference:
- Reports accumulate locally at `~/.cache/ai-skills/reports/<skill>.jsonl`
  (skill-router logs one after every skill use — see its own `.mdc`/
  `SKILL.md`). Summarize with
  `python3 skills/skill-enhancer/scripts/analyze_reports.py <skill-name>`
  (or `--all`).
- No reports yet isn't a failure — fall back to a direct read-through
  audit of the skill's `SKILL.md`/scripts/references against the build
  standard in `skills/skill-router/references/how_to_build_a_new_skill.md`.
- Diagnose root cause before fixing — don't patch the visible symptom.
- Re-verify with the same rigor the skill was originally built with
  (self-tests, validators, skill-creator packaging check, end-to-end
  re-test for anything that touches a tested path).
- Log the change in that skill's own `references/changelog.md`, then
  ship it (commit/push/sync — same checklist as adding a new skill).
- Archive consumed reports with `--archive` so they aren't reprocessed.
- Full procedure: `skills/skill-enhancer/references/
  enhancement_checklist.md`.
